// AN-2 — an abandoning op performed inside a THREADED branch: the thread's
// entry banks the op and its argument area in the task record, the join
// RE-RAISES it in the joiner (first in join order wins), and the unwind
// continues from the join to the install whose arm answers — the arm's
// tuple is the fanout install's value, and the join never delivers the
// branch's dummy. Expected exit: 5. On boot 311479e1 the branch thread
// trapped at the thunk's floor (exit 134).
effect Ab {
  ab() -> Int
}

handler h {
  ab() => (5, 0),
}

fn main() = match (0 <| ({ _ => ab() }, { _ => 10 })) ~> parallel_compose ~> h {
  (a, b) => a + b,
}
